From 599671f5fc1e3a2a38c49e3f7b566954880ce613 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:36:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 185/187] clk: mediatek: acquire MT6897 top mux AP hardware
 votes

Replace the read-only gate behavior for eight top muxes with bounded AP
SET/ACK/DONE/PDN acquisition and CLR/ACK/DONE release. Leave firmware
parent choices and the four VCP IPI muxes read-only. Keep inherited AP
votes until a boot ownership handoff exists and retain own-vote state
through failed rollback or release. Missing voter DT data retains the
read-only fallback.

Adapt the MT6897 vendor protocol, rather than the incompatible FENC mux
helper. This is a new implementation, not an imported vendor commit.

Link: https://github.com/MiCode/MTK_kernel_device_modules/blob/3c4ccd07d5624879555ec710c11bb8818e5cb5c6/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mux.c
Link: https://github.com/MiCode/MTK_kernel_device_modules/blob/3c4ccd07d5624879555ec710c11bb8818e5cb5c6/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6897.c
---
